{"change_summary":"Refactored the substrate-zone update path so `step_substrate_zones` computes, applies, and returns a single `SubstrateOxygenationBreakdown`, letting `engine.rs` reuse that result for tracing instead of recomputing the habitat registry and ROL breakdown twice. Also added the requested inline comment clarifying that `SubstrateSurface` includes the tank footprint top surface, so subtracting `footprint_area_cm2` isolates interstitial grain-matrix area before adding `SubstrateDeep` rootable area.","outstanding_risks":["Validation was targeted rather than full-package: `cargo test -p tank_core` is still blocked by an unrelated existing compile error in `crates/tank_core/tests/denitrification.rs` where `rooted_plants` is undefined, so I validated the touched substrate/root-zone paths with narrower commands instead.","I did not run the full workspace test suite beyond the touched substrate/root-zone coverage."],"steps":[{"description":"Inspect the substrate and engine call flow to confirm where `substrate_oxygenation_breakdown()` was being recomputed and identify the rootable-area subtraction site needing documentation.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Refactor `step_substrate_zones` to return the computed `SubstrateOxygenationBreakdown`, add a shared zero-value helper for early exits, and update engine tracing to use that returned breakdown instead of triggering a second habitat-registry-backed computation.","order":2,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Add the inline physical-meaning comment for the interstitial-area calculation, run formatting, and rerun targeted substrate/root-zone tests to verify the API change preserves behavior.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"validation_evidence":["`cargo fmt --all`","`cargo test -p tank_core --lib systems::substrate::tests -- --nocapture`","`cargo test -p tank_core --test root_zone_oxygenation -- --nocapture`"]}